values ('d2e3f4a5-6b7c-4d62-9e12-2f3a4b5c6d42', 'state-and-local-government', 'State and Local Government', 'Study subnational governance in the American federal system, including state constitutions, federalism, home rule, preemption, grants, and mandates; governors, legislatures, courts, agencies, and judicial selection; municipal forms, counties, special districts, charters, and annexation; state and local elections, parties, redistricting, and direct democracy; local administration, civil service, and service delivery; revenue, budgets, debt, pensions, and fiscal disparities; urban politics, metropolitan governance, and regional inequality; land use, housing, transportation, and infrastructure; public safety, courts, and community well-being; education, health, and human services; climate, emergency management, and local resilience; equity, civil rights, and participation; and state and local data, policy analysis, and transparency.');

