  'State and Local Government',
  'Study subnational governance in the American federal system, including state constitutions, federalism, home rule, preemption, grants, and mandates; governors, legislatures, courts, agencies, and judicial selection; municipal forms, counties, special districts, charters, and annexation; state and local elections, parties, redistricting, and direct democracy; local administration, civil service, and service delivery; revenue, budgets, debt, pensions, and fiscal disparities; urban politics, metropolitan governance, and regional inequality; land use, housing, transportation, and infrastructure; public safety, courts, and community well-being; education, health, and human services; climate, emergency management, and local resilience; equity, civil rights, and participation; and state and local data, policy analysis, and transparency.',
  $slgovjson${"slug": "state-and-local-government", "title": "State and Local Government", "description": "Study subnational governance in the American federal system, including state constitutions, federalism, home rule, preemption, grants, and mandates; governors, legislatures, courts, agencies, and judicial selection; municipal forms, counties, special districts, charters, and annexation; state and local elections, parties, redistricting, and direct democracy; local administration, civil service, and service delivery; revenue, budgets, debt, pensions, and fiscal disparities; urban politics, metropolitan governance, and regional inequality; land use, housing, transportation, and infrastructure; public safety, courts, and community well-being; education, health, and human services; climate, emergency management, and local resilience; equity, civil rights, and participation; and state and local data, policy analysis, and transparency.", "topics": [{"id": "af7a02da-6131-4f54-a5f6-86bfa48f017b", "type": "topic", "title": "State and Local Government in the American Federal System", "description": "Students learn why subnational government is where much of public life is actually governed, funded, delivered, and contested.", "children": [{"id": "efe9a990-a738-4f85-8a88-fa0e3a0bd23e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Why subnational government matters", "children": [{"id": "ee0e3a34-4f7b-4ba5-8721-acfa902627f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Public services, regulation, taxation, and infrastructure"}, {"id": "fc4b5a19-ebff-4f5b-8feb-6d403ed2b415", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy variation across states and cities"}, {"id": "b3c256ea-c8f2-465f-834e-d8cda0a38352", "type": "concept", "title": "Everyday contact between residents and government"}], "description": "The point is to see states and localities as central governing arenas, not secondary versions of national politics."}, {"id": "f492d35b-a9ca-48d0-a64b-faa45239987d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Levels and units of government", "children": [{"id": "2b96108a-7e53-45fb-9160-a6f4d1356018", "type": "concept", "title": "States, counties, municipalities, townships, school districts, and special districts"}, {"id": "9db7bc38-cb07-4764-a129-47f4b5e7dc45", "type": "concept", "title": "Tribal governments and regional authorities"}, {"id": "b381bc4b-883f-4c51-86a0-4176aefdb6da", "type": "concept", "title": "Fragmentation and overlapping jurisdictions"}], "description": "Students learn the range of subnational actors and why their boundaries matter."}, {"id": "ffcc60cd-68b9-4836-af08-7d0bf8188c49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative state/local analysis", "children": [{"id": "9af8c069-a2a9-487b-bfbb-8d198f9d7f1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-state variation"}, {"id": "71c21640-57db-4d78-a4a6-c1be808d8255", "type": "concept", "title": "City-suburb-regional comparison"}, {"id": "4f353b30-9ddd-47e9-be97-55d723b75e26", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy diffusion and learning"}], "description": "A course treats state and local government as a comparative laboratory."}]}, {"id": "b566acfa-818e-42e6-9d6e-25dde8efc022", "type": "topic", "title": "State Constitutions, Federalism, and Intergovernmental Relations", "description": "This module explains the legal and fiscal architecture connecting federal, state, local, tribal, and regional authority.", "children": [{"id": "aa490164-ff1d-4f1d-a3e2-179f8322c807", "type": "subtopic", "title": "State constitutionalism", "children": [{"id": "0fbc05fc-6dad-47cc-a844-9a4af7cb25bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Constitutional amendment processes"}, {"id": "3b064c0e-5d6d-42a4-9c7b-ea41381550ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights provisions and institutional design"}, {"id": "dd8c5a4f-ad5b-4819-b427-8e5ea1f420a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Balanced-budget and tax limitations"}], "description": "State constitutions organize power, rights, fiscal rules, direct democracy, and local authority."}, {"id": "3d34233e-0e54-48dd-8fd5-6177cdf93c4b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Federalism", "children": [{"id": "1acafb61-3faf-4a85-a150-b1a04920d8a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Enumerated, reserved, concurrent, and implied powers"}, {"id": "34bde31c-9a73-455f-8de9-1e872a53061f", "type": "concept", "title": "Preemption and mandates"}, {"id": "3bdc3955-4919-41eb-86df-387a4bb4f2df", "type": "concept", "title": "Cooperative and coercive federalism"}], "description": "Federalism divides and shares power in ways that create both flexibility and conflict."}, {"id": "d352383a-86f2-4149-9be7-8fb142dac67a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intergovernmental relations", "children": [{"id": "181ca1f1-d9d2-4764-8e86-ec8c4b19a943", "type": "concept", "title": "Grants-in-aid and fiscal strings"}, {"id": "3e471941-b08a-4067-9d32-f35122f3451d", "type": "concept", "title": "State-local relations and home rule"}, {"id": "ad5a0b46-31c3-45f5-a83d-0e0cf3562a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional collaboration and conflict"}], "description": "IGR explains how governments coordinate, compete, and bargain."}]}, {"id": "7ed0b086-14aa-4e10-8db8-d3d8dc6a3608", "type": "topic", "title": "State Political Institutions: Governors, Legislatures, Courts, and Agencies", "description": "Students compare the institutions that make, execute, interpret, and administer state policy.", "children": [{"id": "e5b178b2-5fec-4a79-8bb7-9bd3ddf80061", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governors", "children": [{"id": "3702ca06-4b9a-4280-ae11-007f654897d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Vetoes, appointments, budgets, emergency powers, and agenda setting"}, {"id": "b671cf86-1fb6-4d5f-9093-2521219db6a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Lieutenant governors and plural executives"}, {"id": "179a96c4-0d64-4471-8e44-78c4e1a3ace9", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive-legislative bargaining"}], "description": "Students learn how executive power varies across states."}, {"id": "23c1f000-1c41-49d7-92f3-40f9535428c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "State legislatures", "children": [{"id": "cbe78f1c-6562-434d-ba36-11daf0d17b30", "type": "concept", "title": "Professionalization"}, {"id": "c5605c5e-b7ef-4bd7-9a93-ab3fe8a3cc96", "type": "concept", "title": "Committees and leadership"}, {"id": "cd61f82b-07c5-4070-a64e-997df5d05377", "type": "concept", "title": "Term limits and legislative capacity"}], "description": "State legislatures shape law, budgets, oversight, and representation."}, {"id": "bb10987b-ed71-4254-87d9-e1a2a36941ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "State courts and agencies", "children": [{"id": "fb23d4d3-e3da-42d9-8291-deb63ef9b608", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial selection and independence"}, {"id": "b3e92345-55e4-446e-bee1-8b49a289db49", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative agencies and rulemaking"}, {"id": "b571db8f-413e-42dd-81e2-0e07c52e719c", "type": "concept", "title": "Attorney generals, auditors, and secretaries of state"}], "description": "Courts and agencies translate law into decisions, rules, and services."}]}, {"id": "dfc96d65-aef1-48ce-bc8d-9c705face605", "type": "topic", "title": "Local Government Forms, Home Rule, and Municipal Authority", "description": "This topic covers how cities, counties, towns, special districts, and school districts are structured and empowered.", "children": [{"id": "39781404-7960-4577-86fc-6f14078376d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forms of local government", "children": [{"id": "843d1432-bc35-4adf-a7b1-d99761c2df99", "type": "concept", "title": "Mayor-council"}, {"id": "e433dd61-f51a-437c-90b2-3803e8dbe839", "type": "concept", "title": "Council-manager"}, {"id": "7d423ffb-d51c-48dd-97c2-df9016151c39", "type": "concept", "title": "Commission and town meeting forms"}], "description": "Students compare how local institutions organize accountability and expertise."}, {"id": "de01569d-3abd-4fe8-915e-2f237352f1ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Local authority", "children": [{"id": "4999ff58-0fad-44d9-926f-6454bc10347f", "type": "concept", "title": "Dillon's Rule and home rule"}, {"id": "4511abef-2beb-43fa-bdbd-fe3526475c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Charters, ordinances, and local codes"}, {"id": "e024d9d6-1814-4781-8f45-dae7b41172de", "type": "concept", "title": "Annexation, incorporation, and consolidation"}], "description": "Local governments act under state-granted power, which varies widely."}, {"id": "025b853d-73d2-41ee-8d31-8e24828292ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Special districts and counties", "children": [{"id": "a86f332e-0f4c-4d8c-bd8d-0bc7491bb445", "type": "concept", "title": "Counties and county commissions"}, {"id": "5a2e9e5c-6483-4375-acc2-5260e6746a16", "type": "concept", "title": "School boards and school districts"}, {"id": "4a5af9ea-11c1-4daf-8dd1-9cf07535d66d", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, transit, fire, library, and utility districts"}], "description": "Important local functions often sit outside city halls."}]}, {"id": "9ddda651-30f5-4ecc-b9fb-b085d8e57b4c", "type": "topic", "title": "State and Local Elections, Parties, Representation, and Direct Democracy", "description": "Students learn how elections, ballot measures, districts, parties, and participation shape subnational democracy.", "children": [{"id": "8d70f7bb-0c0c-4899-a31c-3885596c51d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Election systems", "children": [{"id": "67bd10b3-e380-4fd6-a4af-b896a722823e", "type": "concept", "title": "At-large, district, and mixed elections"}, {"id": "1b7d8bfd-8d9b-47c9-89a8-e8c19752808a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonpartisan elections and primaries"}, {"id": "74994135-a63c-4041-91bb-99b1d8f88666", "type": "concept", "title": "Ranked choice, runoff, and plurality systems"}], "description": "Students learn how election rules shape who runs, who wins, and who participates."}, {"id": "82975d23-e34f-48c4-9ba2-b9f3595be25d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation", "children": [{"id": "5609f7c9-819c-4dd8-868f-6442969e7349", "type": "concept", "title": "Redistricting and gerrymandering"}, {"id": "f9f1dc95-3453-4677-99a2-648544581041", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive and substantive representation"}, {"id": "3855c570-150f-4dfe-bbc3-8116d49c058d", "type": "concept", "title": "Campaign finance and interest groups"}], "description": "Representation at the subnational level is shaped by districts, turnout, money, and local identities."}, {"id": "1bbb0d75-5e78-4d31-bb77-80e539c556d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Direct democracy", "children": [{"id": "715d42ff-0025-439e-ba5f-7bfdd635cda5", "type": "concept", "title": "Initiatives, referenda, and recalls"}, {"id": "d6230b8f-1f30-41ed-a7f2-4671642b6af0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ballot measure campaigns"}, {"id": "b76fefaf-d884-439a-982d-1e76f2d49839", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits, risks, and administrative complexity"}], "description": "Many states and localities give voters direct lawmaking power."}]}, {"id": "868c4ad0-d612-4600-85d1-d6f56ca1eea6", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Administration, Bureaucracy, and Service Delivery at the Local Level", "description": "This module connects formal institutions to day-to-day administration, frontline work, performance, and public service.", "children": [{"id": "f0032253-a395-45f6-95f4-4ab2ccd3e129", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Administrative structures", "children": [{"id": "40462181-0114-46da-ac10-006d26f5efe5", "type": "concept", "title": "Departments, authorities, boards, and commissions"}, {"id": "96cae8e6-9b0d-4d2b-8dd0-9dbb9839f62d", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil service and personnel systems"}, {"id": "4cd004e3-6415-4b0f-8ab7-0b58e1295fab", "type": "concept", "title": "Contracted and nonprofit service provision"}], "description": "Students connect institutional charts to real service delivery."}, {"id": "968b9ecf-000e-4436-9dd5-a82a6642bc02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Frontline implementation", "children": [{"id": "7ddcb662-0cfd-4813-b9f5-976090de365c", "type": "concept", "title": "Street-level bureaucracy"}, {"id": "20b619ea-4063-42d2-a1fa-10cc0654cc2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility, permitting, inspection, and enforcement"}, {"id": "4387a001-c740-4070-9411-0c92f5a5252a", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative burden and procedural justice"}], "description": "Local policy becomes real through frontline discretion and resident interaction."}, {"id": "9ddf32ec-3427-4852-9284-8e65637a0b21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance and accountability", "children": [{"id": "5b837150-926d-4e1d-b2df-a02130d6e0bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance indicators"}, {"id": "852db99c-623b-43c7-b015-8a2afbfe2b9b", "type": "concept", "title": "311 and service request systems"}, {"id": "52d7357c-59a8-4832-8a71-2078718ee95c", "type": "concept", "title": "Audits, ombuds offices, and resident complaints"}], "description": "Local governments must track service quality while maintaining public trust."}]}, {"id": "8d1be39a-be29-4321-8e09-53d3348eafe6", "type": "topic", "title": "State and Local Public Finance, Budgeting, and Fiscal Federalism", "description": "Students learn how revenue, spending, debt, grants, and fiscal stress shape policy capacity and political choices.", "children": [{"id": "107e7855-a5c0-41d6-b344-5fee926288d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenue systems", "children": [{"id": "0f17489e-3060-47dc-b4e9-7e9967d63155", "type": "concept", "title": "Property, sales, income, and excise taxes"}, {"id": "3de5276a-fa83-48dd-a965-b6ff38cb576d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fees, fines, charges, and special assessments"}, {"id": "e71e6d87-d3e4-4518-96f4-a652cbf84d9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Intergovernmental grants and transfers"}], "description": "Students learn the fiscal tools that fund subnational government."}, {"id": "4677ebd3-e581-4b03-a7a7-a8248a05b6ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Budgeting and fiscal stress", "children": [{"id": "722c9105-be33-4794-98d1-e2a094a13c94", "type": "concept", "title": "Operating and capital budgets"}, {"id": "313c4db9-b1db-4c4f-980a-51105a7e0b83", "type": "concept", "title": "Pensions, debt, and bond ratings"}, {"id": "63c6b068-ee33-417c-933f-3bc53d382693", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiscal stress, bankruptcy, and rainy-day funds"}], "description": "Budgets reveal tradeoffs and constraints."}, {"id": "2a1e07f1-a3c4-48a3-a32d-b429c21480b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity and fiscal federalism", "children": [{"id": "2bb6fe96-2949-43c0-8b45-dd386eede9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax incidence and regressivity"}, {"id": "bf614486-72b4-4640-b3e4-7dfab497508f", "type": "concept", "title": "School finance equalization"}, {"id": "25e0a231-30d5-4689-a25f-167d0cf75d86", "type": "concept", "title": "State aid formulas and local fiscal disparities"}], "description": "Revenue capacity and service needs are uneven across places."}]}, {"id": "bd1a3f87-2bc0-4d76-b2b2-c9fe463744cc", "type": "topic", "title": "Urban Politics, Metropolitan Governance, and Regional Inequality", "description": "This topic studies cities, suburbs, metropolitan coordination, regional fragmentation, and place-based inequality.", "children": [{"id": "a57e43e7-292b-43f9-b31d-36ff61754bd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Urban politics", "children": [{"id": "ac18b2f4-1a2a-4cb9-b504-80e0cbaa07cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mayors, councils, managers, machines, and reform politics"}, {"id": "f3fece40-d136-4ab9-b9ec-1466b4b0e0f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban regimes and growth coalitions"}, {"id": "7ff2fa7c-a295-49f4-be44-cf29c30345f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Community organizations and neighborhood politics"}], "description": "Students learn how cities concentrate political conflict over growth, services, land, and inequality."}, {"id": "ab3470ec-bc90-4cd4-ba46-affd0386b80b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metropolitan governance", "children": [{"id": "722cc3ce-2754-4e85-abbc-af345a8eddff", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional planning organizations"}, {"id": "a030321a-34c4-43b6-a404-b37aadeb28fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Fragmentation and special districts"}, {"id": "23e90309-e84e-45b9-874d-52d81aca0856", "type": "concept", "title": "City-suburb tensions and cooperation"}], "description": "Many problems cross municipal boundaries."}, {"id": "860843b9-286f-45e0-aabd-dc01220e32bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regional inequality", "children": [{"id": "ce3d5d65-e465-458f-95f1-4226edb93e6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregation and concentrated poverty"}, {"id": "a467428d-8d2d-46e6-afd2-bdfb4afc61a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Suburbanization and uneven development"}, {"id": "c180dd2e-7cb6-46cf-97af-106ce3051db8", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional labor markets and service disparities"}], "description": "Place shapes opportunity through housing, schools, jobs, mobility, and tax base."}]}, {"id": "ab55c9d2-d87a-4fa3-a392-40485a5304b6", "type": "topic", "title": "Land Use, Housing, Transportation, and Infrastructure Governance", "description": "Students examine the policy tools that shape where people live, move, work, and access opportunity.", "children": [{"id": "787c4ee5-bebc-4771-b34e-8141d94f8b74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land use", "children": [{"id": "36d4bfe2-4349-47df-9931-e4da6a2174ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning, comprehensive plans, and variances"}, {"id": "2cd44479-67e5-4ca9-bf5d-43d9d4faa5fb", "type": "concept", "title": "NIMBY/YIMBY politics"}, {"id": "21fa01cd-d5c6-4ebf-b7ba-236cb1e0223a", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental review and development approvals"}], "description": "Land-use authority shapes growth, exclusion, environmental risk, and fiscal capacity."}, {"id": "de7cb78d-bfc8-46a2-bdcd-25338a5ccfcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Housing", "children": [{"id": "ddc86792-1b51-4427-8ce4-d7f7215a4374", "type": "concept", "title": "Housing supply and affordability"}, {"id": "63d7f0ea-0292-4b34-a089-7d907c09e4a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Rent regulation, vouchers, and public housing"}, {"id": "f80621c3-5cd5-41a8-8023-2248eab0af70", "type": "concept", "title": "Fair housing and exclusionary zoning"}], "description": "Housing policy links local rules to affordability, segregation, homelessness, and mobility."}, {"id": "7baab572-bdd2-42cf-8647-823d7d215c01", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and transportation", "children": [{"id": "34711d96-c294-418b-88a3-f98098a9676e", "type": "concept", "title": "Roads, transit, water, stormwater, and broadband"}, {"id": "782056c8-f077-485e-be91-48ea598fcf76", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital planning and asset management"}, {"id": "d99398bc-0952-437f-83c1-d2cf6df3aeaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobility equity and complete streets"}], "description": "Infrastructure decisions shape economic opportunity and climate resilience."}]}, {"id": "4a74e5ea-1590-443b-a161-d5ae57ca30e0", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Safety, Courts, Criminal Justice, and Community Well-Being", "description": "This module covers the local governance of policing, courts, corrections, emergency response, and public safety reform.", "children": [{"id": "d3a3a450-f111-4f42-af2c-222a23a65c65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public safety institutions", "children": [{"id": "116245a9-84de-4b74-b8e6-3ff5f5f6dfea", "type": "concept", "title": "Police, sheriffs, prosecutors, courts, jails, probation, and emergency medical services"}, {"id": "51b7e395-d9b9-410c-9e15-8e7e72e16d34", "type": "concept", "title": "State criminal law and local enforcement"}, {"id": "3d91ee1d-134a-4389-afc3-38ed3ff4ea71", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination across agencies"}], "description": "States and localities govern most everyday criminal justice institutions."}, {"id": "2353629f-2c5e-40ca-9246-3ef005477798", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reform and accountability", "children": [{"id": "3874c159-707a-46e8-8167-5a8e5f0c7e97", "type": "concept", "title": "Use-of-force policy and civilian oversight"}, {"id": "70f44eb4-b42d-487d-b56b-f930a14081a4", "type": "concept", "title": 